WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.580
The world of science fiction is endless and
there's no shortage of new stories to tell.

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:07.740
But sometimes, the best sci-fi stories on
television are the ones you've never even

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:08.240
heard of.

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:13.820
Set in a small German town, Dark is a sci-fi
thriller where strange, supernatural occurrences

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:16.980
have exposed secrets hiding in the closets
of several families.

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:21.020
"Hi, nanny. Hi, grampy.”

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:26.760
More than living up to its title, the show
includes scenes of adultery, kidnapping, and

00:00:26.770 --> 00:00:31.550
homicide. Plus, it's all set against the backdrop
of time travel. This Netflix series is a slow

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:35.740
burn and, at times, the physics of Dark's
time travel can be a little hard to follow.

00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:40.500
But when it all comes into focus, the emotional
impact of the larger storyline is worth every

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:41.620
second of the journey.

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:43.700
"Welcome to the future."

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:48.820
Fans of Superman will find many reasons to
binge Syfy's prequel series Krypton. Set two

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:52.960
generations before the destruction of the
Man of Steel's home planet, the show focuses

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:57.640
on Superman's grandfather and on the choices
he must make to ensure his grandson's future

00:00:57.660 --> 00:00:58.400
survival.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:04.280
In its second season, Krypton started introducing
some DC fan favorites into the mix, including

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:08.610
Lobo, an intergalactic bounty hunter in the
same gritty vein as Marvel's Wolverine and

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:09.880
Punisher...only much cooler.

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:11.900
"Please stop, you’re making me blush."

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:16.240
Although most comic-book geeks already know
how the story turns out, Syfy has found a

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:20.500
way to deliver enough surprises to keep even
the most hardcore Super-fans guessing about

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:21.720
what will happen next.

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:27.630
The Expanse is based on a series of novels
by James S. A. Corey and follows a group of

00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:32.530
future antiheroes in a space-colonized world
on the verge of war. Often compared to Battlestar

00:01:32.530 --> 00:01:36.820
Galactica, The Expanse is a sort of space
opera that not only delivers a compelling

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:40.580
story but benefits from special effects that
don't feel like they belong on basic cable.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:41.200
"Meow."

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:45.960
Luckily, if you didn't get a chance to catch
the show before it was cancelled by Syfy,

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:50.340
another network is giving the series a second
life. Following a huge "save-The-Expanse"

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:53.590
social media campaign, Amazon stepped in and
picked up the show.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:55.580
"We just dodged a massive bullet."

00:01:56.280 --> 00:02:00.619
In Netflix's The Society, a group of teens
return to their hometown to discover that

00:02:00.619 --> 00:02:04.799
it's been mysteriously dropped into the middle
of nowhere — with no adults, no outside

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:06.969
resources and, worst of all, no internet.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:08.700
"What? Nah. Come on."

00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:13.470
Thrown into a reality where technology no
longer exists, these teens not only need to

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:17.780
adapt, they need to grow up far faster than
anyone should. Like a mash-up between Lord

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:22.480
of the Flies, and Lost, The Society says as
much about humanity as it does about technology.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:28.030
The OA feels like nothing else that's come
before it. The show centers on a young woman

00:02:28.030 --> 00:02:32.830
who reappears after having been kept in captivity
for seven years. But unlike most captives,

00:02:32.830 --> 00:02:35.440
she has the ability to travel through parallel
dimensions.

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:40.140
This supernatural, sci-fi thriller is packed
with surprises. From questioning its main

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:44.220
character's mental state to throwing a huge
curveball at the end of its sophomore run,

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:49.480
The OA has taken nearly every twist and turn
a proper science fiction series can take...including

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:51.550
a guest spot from a telepathic octopus.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:53.580
"What the f--- is this?”

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:55.400
“I just do the lights, bro."

00:02:56.220 --> 00:03:00.360
Unfortunately, future episodes won't be twisting
and turning on Netflix — the streaming service

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:05.240
decided to end its involvement with the series
after its second season. But with a "save-the-OA"

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:09.340
campaign in full swing, one never knows when
or where the show might resurface.

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:19.160
Despite a few surface similarities to Rick
and Morty, Final Space is a show all its own.

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:24.140
This animated sci-fi comedy on Adult Swim
is the demented brain-child of Olan Rogers

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:29.071
— with a little help from executive producer
Conan O'Brien. It's centered on the space

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:34.560
adventures of Gary Godspeed and his planet-destroying
alien friend, Mooncake. Along for the ride

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:39.400
is a rag-tag group of intergalactic characters,
ranging from a cat-like bounty hunter to a

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:41.570
robot companion voiced by Fred Armisen.

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:45.840
"Hey, Gary! My name is Kevin, I’m your deep
space sanity avoidance companion. Nice to

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:46.580
meet you.”

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:47.700
“I already hate you."

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:51.840
The show's lighthearted tone perfectly balances
its often thoughtful storylines. While it

00:03:51.860 --> 00:03:55.940
may take a few episodes to sort things out,
it's worth the trip and trippiness to see

00:03:55.940 --> 00:03:56.580
it through.

00:03:57.620 --> 00:04:02.400
Imagine if The Chronicles of Narnia and Harry
Potter were written for adults. The result

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:07.510
would be Syfy's The Magicians. This intelligent,
fun, and remarkably relevant series deals

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:11.040
with complex themes while dropping pop culture
references at every turn.

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:13.580
"You watch Battlestar, right?”

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:17.880
“Yeah, I love when they do terrorism allegory
with mostly white people.”

00:04:18.220 --> 00:04:23.200
It's from the creative mind of Sera Gamble,
who spent over a decade on the CW's Supernatural.

00:04:23.470 --> 00:04:27.340
The overall tone of the show is similar to
Supernatural but The Magicians deals with

00:04:27.350 --> 00:04:32.060
more adult subject matter. And it does so
in a way that's conscious and inclusive...while

00:04:32.060 --> 00:04:34.140
also throwing in the occasional epic magic
battle.

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:38.140
The premise of Future Man sounds a lot like
something that would have been featured in

00:04:38.220 --> 00:04:43.220
a 1960s TV show — an underachieving janitor
travels back in time to save the world. But

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:47.660
in the hands of Seth Rogen and Evan Goldberg,
this simple time travel comedy turns into

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:52.100
a brilliant, star-studded misadventure that
pays homage to our greatest sci-fi films.

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:53.100
"The Matrix”

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:53.760
“Back to the Future.”

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:54.300
“Star Wars.”

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:54.840
“Terminator.”

00:04:54.840 --> 00:04:55.840
“Mad Max."

00:04:56.080 --> 00:05:00.200
Despite the show's second season receiving
a 100% Fresh rating on Rotten Tomatoes, Deadline

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:05.500
announced in April 2019 that Future Man would
call it quits after its third season on Hulu.

00:05:05.970 --> 00:05:10.160
While Future Man might soon be a thing of
the past, it's guaranteed to go out with a

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:12.540
bang...and it just might save the world in
the process.

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:17.990
Philip K. Dick's Electric Dreams features
an approach to anthology storytelling similar

00:05:17.990 --> 00:05:22.820
to Black Mirror. Where the Amazon series differs
is in its more optimistic outlook on the future.

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:27.560
Drawing from various short stories by the
man who created Blade Runner and The Man in

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:31.400
the High Castle, Electric Dreams doesn't actually
believe the future is without hope.

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:34.080
"The future ain’t what it used to be."

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:39.560
Delivering stories that span vastly different
time periods, the series creates extraordinarily

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:44.730
diverse settings that explore technology in
wildly different ways. The result is modern,

00:05:44.730 --> 00:05:49.290
but also tangible. Electric Dreams feels like
a reality that could actually happen, and

00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:50.380
that isn't such a bad thing.

